 "page": [
  {
   "kind": "town",
   "label": "town",
   "section": "header",
   "text": "Hochhausen · village · germanic · threat frontier · route road · terrain river · seed sim-village"
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "historicalCharacter",
   "section": "identity",
   "text": "Older residents still distinguish between 'the original settlement' and 'what we have now'. The Siege is where that line falls, not a clean line, but a real one"
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-13",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.market",
   "pool": "MARKET-OPEN",
   "section": "site",
   "text": "A stranger finds Hochhausen's market without directions, because the busiest way through town leads there on its own.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-17",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.institutions",
   "pool": "GARRISONED",
   "section": "site",
   "text": "Armed order is part of Hochhausen's furniture; the town keeps professionals for its safety rather than trusting to luck and neighbours.",
   "vid": 0
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "prosperity",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Comfortable"
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "safetyLabel",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Moderate"
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "readiness",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Lightly Defended"
  },
  {
   "kind": "badge",
   "label": "foodSecurity",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Secure"
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "prosperity: Comfortable / Prosperous",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "People in Hochhausen can afford to argue about things other than money.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "economicViability.viable: true",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Hochhausen is a town that works: what it needs, it can get, and what it makes, it can move.",
   "vid": 0
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "defenseProfile.readiness.label: Lightly Defended",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "What Hochhausen could hold, it could hold briefly.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.military: ADEQUATE",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Hochhausen would hold against what it expects, and it knows it is not proof against what it does not.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.monster: WEAK",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Nothing at Hochhausen is organised against what lives outside the fields; each household answers for its own fences.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.internal: WEAK",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Hochhausen's complaint book has more entries opened in it than closed.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.economic: WEAK",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "There is nothing spare in Hochhausen, and the absence of spare is what a careful eye notices first.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "scores.magical: CRITICAL",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Hochhausen keeps no practitioner, no arrangement, and no expectation of either.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-3",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.systemsHealth",
   "pool": "foodSecurity.label: Secure",
   "section": "health",
   "text": "Hochhausen's security is its own harvest, which means it is proof against a closed road and not against a bad year.",
   "vid": 3
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-2",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.conflicts",
   "pool": "intensity: low",
   "section": "tensions",
   "text": "You would not learn from a day in Hochhausen that The Commercial Circle and The Administrative Circle are at odds. It comes up on the second day.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "arrivalScene",
   "section": "situation",
   "text": "Hochhausen is ordinary in the best sense: a place where people live and work and argue and sleep, which is most of what places are for. A proper village, large enough to have a market and small enough that strangers are noticed: steep roofs, enclosed craft yards, and carved lintels mark the older wards. A magelight lamp post marks the main gate. Hochhausen is announced by the smoke of its cookfires and the sound of its market before its buildings are visible."
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "pressureSentence",
   "section": "situation",
   "text": "Elected Reeve has been debating market levies for three months. The merchants have stopped attending the sessions. Both sides are now acting as if the other has already lost."
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-5",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.situation",
   "pool": "ordinary (route road and the default)",
   "section": "situation",
   "text": "Goods come into Hochhausen and goods go out of it, and neither the coming nor the going is remarkable.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-6",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.origin",
   "pool": "road",
   "section": "origin",
   "text": "Hochhausen is on a road and lives off the road: goods in, goods out, people through.",
   "vid": 0
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-6",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.origin",
   "pool": "tier overlay: other tiers",
   "section": "origin",
   "text": "Hochhausen is the size that a place of this kind settles at, and it has settled there.",
   "vid": 0
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-REL-2",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.notableConnection",
   "pool": "prominentRelationship present",
   "section": "connection",
   "text": "One of Hochhausen's ties carries more weight than the rest, and the weight shows in what the town will and will not do.",
   "vid": 1
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-REL-2",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.notableConnection",
   "pool": "flagDriven count zero",
   "section": "connection",
   "text": "The people of Hochhausen are connected the way the people of any settled place are connected, and there is no more to say about it than that.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "kind": "machine",
   "label": "prominentRelationship",
   "section": "connection",
   "text": "Ingrid Köhler and Ivo Werner are connected by something neither discusses openly: A third party has asked Ingrid Köhler, quietly, whether Ivo Werner can be trusted. The answer took too long."
  },
  {
   "block": "DS-GEN-7",
   "face": 0,
   "kind": "composed",
   "mount": "overview.warnings",
   "pool": "structuralSuggestions[]",
   "section": "warnings",
   "text": "A careful reader of Hochhausen finds one loose end, and it is the kind that a single institution would tie off.",
   "vid": 2
  },
  {
   "kind": "roster",
   "label": "institutions",
   "section": "institutions",
   "text": "institutions: Multiple water sources, Dwellings (80-180), Farmland, Weekly market, Mill, Blacksmith, Carpenter, Thatcher, Cooper, Bowyer & fletcher, Sawmill, Stone quarry, Potter, Tailor, Woodcarver, Cartographer's workshop, Parish church, Priest (resident), Graveyard, Village reeve, Adventurers' charter hall, Veteran's lodge, Underground network, Alehouse, Maltster, Fish market, Fuller, Brickmaker, Common grazing land"
  }
 ],
